Wednesday Update
* Trade Alert: Exited AAL puts. Buy GM and DY calls*&nbsp;Stocks slammed on=
 new bond yields fearStocks are swirling lower today asa investors react to=
 a renewed uptick in bond yields.Through 2:30 pm ET, the Dow was down 0.1% =
after being up as much as 0.3%, the S&amp;P 500 is down 1%, the Nasdaq 100 =
is down 2.8% and the Smallcap 600 is up 0.4%.The broader markets have retre=
ated following Monday's sharp rally, extending recent volatility on the pro=
spects of rising rates as the economy reopens amid falling COVID-19 infecti=
ons. Still, all three indexes are sitting not too far from the record level=
s struck last month.President Joe Biden said Tuesday that all adult America=
ns will be able to receive a coronavirus vaccine by the end of May, two mon=
ths earlier than previously anticipated.In the bond market, the US 10-year =
Treasury yield ticked up to 1.489% from 1.405% on Tuesday. It climbed to a =
one-year high last week following a change in inflation expectations on the=
 back of improving economic data.Meanwhile, Lyft (LYFT) climbed to the high=
est level since July 2019 after the ride-share company posted improving rid=
ership last month and narrowed its Q1 operating loss forecast. The stock ju=
mped about 9% midday.Cruise operators shares also climbed up sharply on the=
 US vaccination plans. Carnival (CCL),Royal Caribbean (RCL) and Norwegian C=
ruise Line (NCLH) rose between 4% and 7%. Airline stocks were also higher, =
including American Airlines (AAL) and United Airlines (UAL).In contrast, ma=
jor tech stocks continued to weaken, with Apple (AAPL), Amazon (AMZN) and M=
icrosoft (MSFT) all lower.On the energy front, oil prices rose, with US Wes=
t Texas Intermediate up 3.25% to $61.69 per barrel on optimism surrounding =
vaccinations, but gains were capped by a buildup in US crude stockpiles.Por=
tfolio: &nbsp;We sold our AAL puts at $1.75 on stop, unfortunately. Our ord=
er for GM calls did not fill.&nbsp; We have two new ideas for you.*CURRENT =
RECOMMENDATIONSAmerican Airlines Group (AAL) March $23 puts-- Symbol: AAL21=
0319P00023000-- Bought at $2.40 on Monday-- Sold on stop today for a 27% lo=
ss.*NEW RECOMMENDATIONS&nbsp;Dycom Industries (DY) March 85 calls-- Symbol:=
 DY210319C00085000-- Order: Buy at $4.00 lmt day only-- If filled, set up t=
o sell half at $5.20 lmt gtc and half at $6.80 lmt gtc-- If filled, set sto=
p at $2.80 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*General Motors March 50 calls=
-- Symbol: GM210319C00050000-- Order: Buy at $4.10 lmt day only-- If filled=
, set up to sell half at $5.30 lmt gtc and half at $7.00 lmt gtc-- If fille=
d, set stop at $2.90 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,=
Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the t=
hird Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are go=
od after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are=
 good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at =
the close of the current session. Past results are no guarantee of future r=
eturns. All accounts may not achieve comparable results. Recommendations ar=
